            <div xml:id="d426">

                <pb facs="0644" n="556" sameAs="frus:frus1892/pg556"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hirsch to Mr.
                            Blaine.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-04-08"><hi rendition="#italic">April 8, 1892</hi></date>.
                        (Received April 25.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 424.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The letter of Rev. H. O. Dwight of March
                    29, sent to the Department as an inclosure in my No. 423 of this date, concludes
                    with another instance of tampering with letters of American citizens, which I
                    have reported to the Department in a previous communication. I at once renewed
                    my former complaint to the grand vizier, who again promised to correct the
                    evil.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Solomon Hirsch.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
